    {
      "id": 221516,
      "name": "MindWanderer",
      "username": "MindWanderer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/{size}/4816_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-08-20T02:26:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"robertmaxfreeman\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/robertmaxfreeman/48/2147_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> robertmaxfreeman:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Parse’s Buffer Overflow doesn’t work on Scions, because the Scions aren’t villain cards. Villain cards come from villain decks.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Incorrect. Lead From the Front only works on damage from villain cards, for instance, and of course it works on damage from any villain character card. It doesn’t work because they aren’t entering play, they’re already in play. So Updated Intel would also not work.</p>",
